WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Speaker 1: We now have learned about yet another&nbsp;
fraud perpetrated on you, the American taxpayer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:11.160
by Donald Trump and his family. The Washington&nbsp;
Post is now reporting Donald Trump charged the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:16.920
Secret Service exorbitant rates at his hotels.&nbsp;
This was another grift in order to make money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:24.060
Listen to this. Records show that in&nbsp;
40 cases, the Trump Organization billed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.580
the Secret Service far higher amounts than&nbsp;
the approved government rate. In one case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:37.680
charging agents 1100 $85 a night to stay&nbsp;
at the Trump International Hotel in D.C..&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.060
The new billing documents, according&nbsp;
to a congressional committees review,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:51.060
show that taxpayers paid the president's company&nbsp;
at least $1.4 million for Secret Service agents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:57.900
stays at Trump properties for his and his family's&nbsp;
protection. The records, by the way, contradict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:03.720
the repeated claim made by Eric Trump, the&nbsp;
president's son, and the Trump. Org's executive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.980
vice president, that the family's company often&nbsp;
gave the Secret Service agents the hotel rooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:16.260
at cost or free. Maybe it was sometimes true, but&nbsp;
it often was not. This is the latest grift on you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.700
the American people. This is, by the way,&nbsp;
sometimes this is used as a way to money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:27.540
to launder money, which is like the real price of&nbsp;
something is 400 bucks, but you start billing 1200&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:33.180
bucks and then you can launder $800. That's not&nbsp;
apparently what's going on here. Here, it's just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.100
a form of fraud. Listen, the hotel room is worth&nbsp;
400 bucks. We're going to charge the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:45.660
1200 bucks a night. We will direct Secret&nbsp;
Service to stay at these rooms and then taxpayers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:51.120
are going to pay for it. And it is another&nbsp;
complete and total grift. And, of course, oh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:58.440
Trump donated his paycheck. Okay. $400,000 a year.&nbsp;
Look at the millions upon millions of dollars. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:04.380
you look at all the hotels that were made on&nbsp;
the back of Trump being president, remember,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:09.060
the other side of this was foreign leaders staying&nbsp;
at Trump properties when they went to D.C. or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.820
elsewhere to ingratiate themselves with Donald&nbsp;
Trump. So it has been a scam after scam after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:20.280
scam. Extremely profitable, despite Trump's claim.&nbsp;
Oh, I could have made a bunch more money. Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:25.620
made plenty of money while he was president. And&nbsp;
so the fact that he donated his $400,000 salary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:30.900
really is neither here nor there. Added on to&nbsp;
the list of more investigations that will be done

